      "text": "The cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzyme family is the primary metabolic system for drugs. CYP enzymes are the source of most clinically significant drug-drug interactions (DDIs) and the target of pharmacogenomic variation that explains why patients respond differently to the same drug."
